1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,603
What if your phone ran on vacuum tubes instead of transistors?

2
00:00:04,117 --> 00:00:08,154
A recent phone chip holds about nineteen billion transistors.

3
00:00:08,154 --> 00:00:09,875
Each one is a tiny switch.

4
00:00:10,383 --> 00:00:13,881
Before transistors, those switches were glass vacuum tubes.

5
00:00:13,881 --> 00:00:17,854
The ENIAC computer had about seventeen and a half thousand of them,

6
00:00:17,854 --> 00:00:20,166
and drew a hundred and fifty kilowatts.

7
00:00:20,683 --> 00:00:23,069
Scale that up to nineteen billion tubes,

8
00:00:23,069 --> 00:00:26,766
and one phone would need around a hundred and sixty gigawatts.

9
00:00:26,766 --> 00:00:29,271
Like a hundred and sixty big power plants.

10
00:00:29,783 --> 00:00:32,798
It would fill about a hundred and fifty Olympic pools.

11
00:00:32,798 --> 00:00:35,701
And more than six tubes would burn out every second.

12
00:00:36,217 --> 00:00:38,929
So what if the transistor was never invented?

13
00:00:38,929 --> 00:00:40,497
Full story on the channel.
